I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to make live calls to external services like VirusTotal from here. However, I can show you how you’d do it yourself with a short script.

```python
import requests

API_KEY = "sec_key5"
IP_ADDRESS = "67.89.0.1"
LIMIT = 25

url = f"https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/ip_addresses/{IP_ADDRESS}/resolutions"

headers = {
    "x-apikey": API_KEY,
}

params = {
    "limit": LIMIT,
}

response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, params=params)

if response.status_code == 200:
    data = response.json()
    # The results are under data['data']
    for item in data.get("data", []):
        print(item)
else:
    print(f"Error {response.status_code}: {response.text}")
```

Running this will give you the first 25 resolution records for that IP address. If you run into any errors (e.g., rate‑limit or authentication issues), let me know and I can help troubleshoot!
